# Scratch — screenshots Briggsy drops for review, agent debris. Never committed.
temp/
temp-*

# War-room scratch, written into draft-kit/ during a live draft or mock and read by
# draft_engine.py from its cwd. Per-draft state, worthless the moment the draft ends.
draft-kit/picks.json
draft-kit/new_picks.json
draft-kit/slot_names.json

# Discarded Imagen rolls + superseded avatar variants. Kept on disk as the visual
# record of how the logos got made; too heavy (30MB of 2-3MB PNGs) to carry in history.
# The two keepers — logo/deez-nuts/ and logo/hunter-maker/ — ARE tracked.
logo/archive/

# Watcher state is per-machine runtime, not source. last_seen.json is the diff baseline (it
# changes every hour, on every machine, and means nothing to anyone else) and DRAFT_ALERTS.md is
# local output Briggsy reads. Committing either would rewrite the repo hourly for zero value --
# same reasoning as the inbox below. .gitkeep so a clean clone still has somewhere to write.
newsletter/data/state/*
!newsletter/data/state/.gitkeep

# Mule cargo is a CACHE, not source: the hourly job overwrites every file in inbox/
# (the two RSS feeds alone churn ~1.2MB an hour) and the newsletter build drains it
# into data/archive/. Committing either would rewrite the repo every hour for zero value.
# Both directories keep a .gitkeep so a clean clone still has somewhere to land cargo.
newsletter/data/inbox/*
!newsletter/data/inbox/.gitkeep
newsletter/data/archive/*
!newsletter/data/archive/.gitkeep

# nflverse weekly stats are a CACHE, not source: ~1.6MB per season, six seasons on disk, and
# every byte is re-downloadable from a versioned GitHub release. `draft-kit/cache/` itself is
# NOT ignored -- sleeper_players.json.gz lives there and IS committed, because U14's frozen ids
# are only meaningful against the exact dump they were resolved from.
# The oracle these feed is committed instead, at tests/fixtures/player_stats_2024_reg.csv.gz
# (one real season, 324KB gzipped), so the scoring tests survive a clean clone.
draft-kit/cache/player_stats_*.csv
# Play-by-play is the same deal, an order of magnitude larger (~19MB/season
# gzipped). It is the route to the 2025 season and the long-TD bonuses; see
# the docstring in scripts/build_curves.py before fetching it again.
draft-kit/cache/play_by_play_*.csv.gz
